abstract: >-
  Kinship is a dependency-free TypeScript control plane that decides what an AI agent fleet may
  do to reach a person, and proves that it was decided. The runtime produces approval cards
  and an append-only, replayable audit log; it ships no channel transport, so nothing
  member-facing can send. Governance is enforced by tested code rather than by prose, and every
  refusal is a record rather than a crash.
